	"bugClass": {
		"id": "shared-file-clobber",
		"title": "Shared output file overwritten without ownership validation",
		"cause": "A process writes to a default or shared filesystem path and replaces existing contents without verifying that the file belongs to the same database, instance, or owner. Related status reporting reads a persisted success record rather than validating the current file on disk, so it can report success after the file has been replaced or emptied.",
		"criteria": "Classify another site when runtime code writes, copies, renames, or atomically replaces a file at a shared or default-derived path without checking the existing file's owner or data identity. Also admit cases where status is derived only from a stored success/state record and does not inspect the artifact it claims is current. Either mechanism is sufficient when it can produce the reported stale or clobbered artifact.",
